## Home

**Home** is the first page after you sign in. It has:

- A message box, **What's on your mind today?**. Type a request and press Enter: Operon opens a chat with the AI employee you named, or with the first AI employee that takes free messages.
- A line with the number of your unread chat messages.
- **AI Employees**: a card for each AI employee you can use. Point at a card to show **Chat** and **Detail**.

Which AI employees you see depends on what your firm has enabled and on your role. If you see **No AI employees are available to your account** or **No AI employees are enabled yet**, ask your tenant admin.

### For tenant admins: Finish setting up

A tenant admin sees the card **Finish setting up** until the firm's set-up is complete. Each row shows **Done** or **To do**, and **Configure** opens the page where it is done:

| Step | Done when |
|---|---|
| **Enable AI employees** | At least one AI employee is enabled. |
| **Invite your colleagues** | The firm has at least two users. |
| **Grant suite access to your team** | Every enabled suite has been granted to at least one department or user. Shown when such a suite is enabled. |
| **Set a default secretary profile** | The Secretary suite has a default profile. Shown when the secretary AI employee is enabled. |

**Dismiss** hides the card for you in this browser.

## Open a chat

You can open a chat with an AI employee from:

- the card on **Home**, with **Chat**;
- the message box on **Home**;
- the employee's **Detail** page, with **Start Conversation**;
- the **Team** page, with **Chat** on the employee's card;
- **My agents** in the side bar of a workspace.

The left panel of the chat shows the employee and three sections, one open at a time:

| Section | Use |
|---|---|
| **Workflows** | The workflows this employee runs. Select ▶ to start one. Some AI employees only work through workflows: then the message box says **Start a workflow from the Workflows panel to chat**. |
| **My Tasks** | Tasks from this employee's workflows: **Assigned** to you, and **Completed**. |
| **History** | Your earlier conversations, with search. Select **New chat** to start a new conversation; use the delete button on a conversation to remove it. |

## Send a message

Type in **Type a message...** and press Enter. Shift+Enter starts a new line.

**Attachments.** When the message box is empty, select **+** and choose **Photo** or **File**. You can also paste an image.

| | Types | Size | Per message |
|---|---|---|---|
| Images | PNG, JPEG, GIF, WebP | up to 5 MB each | up to 4 |
| Files | PDF, Word, PowerPoint, Excel, CSV, text, Markdown | up to 15 MB each | up to 3 |

Only the first 100,000 characters of a long file are read. Scanned files of more than 20 pages or 5 MB are not accepted.

**While the employee replies**, the send button becomes **Stop**; select it to stop the reply. A **Thinking…** panel shows the employee's reasoning; afterwards it folds into **Thought process**, which you can expand. When the employee searches the web, its **Sources** are listed under the reply.

**Reply language.** The AI employee replies in the language of your last message: write in Chinese and it answers in Chinese, write in English and it answers in English. The interface language does not change this.

{% aside type="caution" %}
AI employees can make mistakes. Check important information — figures, dates, names and anything that will be filed or sent to a client — before you rely on it.
{% /aside %}

## Confirm what the employee proposes

Before an AI employee does something that changes data — for example, creating records or sending something — it shows a card with what it will do, marked **Awaiting confirmation**. Each item is marked **Will run**, **Skip** or **Not allowed**, and **⚠ Cannot be undone** marks actions that cannot be reversed.

- Select **Run it** to let the employee go ahead. The card shows **Running…** and then **Done**, with the result of each item.
- Select **Cancel** to stop it.

A card that is not confirmed lapses: if you send a new message, or after 30 minutes. Ask the employee again if you still want it done.

Some steps need an approval from a colleague. They appear as an **APPROVAL** card with **Approve**, **Reject**, **Transfer** and **Add Approver**.

## Tell us about a reply

Under a reply, select **Helpful** or **Something's wrong**, choose the reasons, add a comment if you like, and select **Send**. Your feedback helps us improve the AI employees.
